# Appfile — app + account identifiers, loaded by every lane in the Fastfile.
#
# Secrets policy (architecture.md §9): ZERO credentials live in this repo.
# The Apple Developer / App Store Connect identifiers below stay commented and
# are injected at release time (M6, release.yml) from GitHub environment
# secrets — never committed here.

app_identifier("com.beyondkaira.hayati")  # iOS bundle id — renamed S037; com.hayati.app was squatted on Apple (ADR-027)

# --- All three stay COMMENTED: App Store Connect API-key auth needs none of
# them (the key is team-scoped). Kept as documentation of what a
# password/Apple-ID lane would have required.
#
# They are NOT equivalent, and grouping them under one "never commit" rule was
# over-broad (corrected S041, ADR-029 D1):
#   apple_id    — the founder's EMAIL. Never commit: PII, and a phishing target.
#   itc_team_id — an internal App Store Connect numeric id. No public artifact
#                 carries it and nothing needs it here; no reason to commit.
#   team_id     — the Apple Developer portal Team ID. An IDENTIFIER, not a
#                 credential: it is published in every distributed IPA's
#                 embedded provisioning profile, it grants nothing without the
#                 private key, and it already appears in four repo documents.
#                 It IS committed — as `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` in
#                 `app/ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj`, where xcodebuild
#                 actually needs it, pinned by
#                 `app/test/release/signing_sentinel_test.dart`.
#
# architecture.md §9's "zero keys in repo" is untouched by any of this.
# apple_id("...")
# itc_team_id("...")

# No Android block here: Play account credentials (json_key_file) arrive with
# the Android lanes in M6.5 (ADR-006).
